arget\":{\"target_id\":\"sha256:a5c1daee7886f81d27b2b7718718fa7a3822b27a4bc1d057f99af01be7688a19\",\"display_path\":\"/Users/arndtgold/Documents/GitHub/ai-native-governance-delivery-framework\"},\"snapshot_id\":\"78ad8574-75b4-497a-bdf6-286ad7972052\",\"observed_as_of\":\"2026-10-18T09:57:49.334Z\",\"source_digest\":\"189274a610b9b56c914baa095648f51cba1115f4a03c6eaea2f5b861a3932917\",\"state\":\"available\",\"code\":null,\"retryable\":false,\"data\":{\"context_id\":\"9864e966-112a-44da-9e36-f95521009ec5\",\"generation\":10,\"current\":true},\"authorizes\":false}}}}" sandboxId=source-66635fa41555d0fc sourceId=undefined
2026-10-18T09:57:50.916Z warning [mcp-app-sandbox] mcp_app_sandbox.console_message guestWebContentsId=8 initId=ad0aa791-a14d-468f-aecb-b474fce3868b level=warning lineNumber=105 message="AGDF_SDK_TRACE {\"trace_id\":\"e1978ebc-f2e2-4076-88c5-a63e0b036e56\",\"sequence\":26,\"observed_at\":\"2026-10-18T09:57:50.915Z\",\"direction\":\"out\",\"message\":{\"method\":\"ui/update-model-context\",\"params\":{\"structuredContent\":{\"schema_version\":\"1\",\"target\":{\"target_id\":\"sha256:a5c1daee7886f81d27b2b7718718fa7a3822b27a4bc1d057f99af01be7688a19\",\"display_path\":\"/Users/arndtgold/Documents/GitHub/ai-native-governance-delivery-framework\"},\"snapshot_id\":\"78ad8574-75b4-497a-bdf6-286ad7972052\",\"observed_as_of\":\"2026-10-18T09:57:49.334Z\",\"source_digest\":\"189274a610b9b56c914baa095648f51cba1115f4a03c6eaea2f5b861a3932917\",\"run_id\":\"agdf-cockpit-plugin-integration-20261016-01\",\"revision_id\":\"641e88e1-6bf4-4712-a01f-887d6d045fa2\",\"context_id\":\"9864e966-112a-44da-9e36-f95521009ec5\",\"generation\":10,\"prepared_at\":\"2026-10-18T09:57:50.528Z\",\"artefact\":{\"resource\":{\"resource_id\":\"c9a3e8ad-8768-48fb-bc48-3f14283a99e4\",\"run_id\":\"agdf-cockpit-plugin-integration-20261016-01\",\"type\":\"PRD\",\"path\":\".agdf/control/artefacts/agdf-cockpit-plugin-integration-20261016-01/PRD.md\",\"registered_reference\":\".agdf/control/artefacts/agdf-cockpit-plugin-integration-20261016-01/PRD.md\",\"status\":\"registered\"},\"format\":\"markdown\",\"content\":\"# PRD: Cockpit included in the AGDF plugin for Codex\\n\\nStatus: draft\\nGate: PRD\\nGate approval: open\\nBased on: approved UR\\nDate: 2026-10-16\\nOwner: Arndt Gold\\nTraceability contract: criteria-chain-v1\\n\\n## 1. Product Scope\\n\\nDeliver the existing Cockpit as part of the normal AGDF plugin installation in Codex. The user installs or updates AGDF and asks to open Cockpit for an established project; no separate Cockpit build, MCP registration or project configuration is required. The visible feature name is **Cockpit**, identified as part of AGDF where its host surface supports that identification. Technical tool/server identifiers remain an SD compatibility decision.\\n\\nInstallation and opening must distinguish supplied, enabled, connected and actually working states. A confirmed project is required for reading project data. Existing local users get a controlled transition, with verified replacement before retirement of a positively owned old connection. The product does not promise that host trust, permission or restart requirements disappear.\\n\\nFirst scope is Codex, including bounded local installation and fresh-host verification. Existing Claude work remains separate. Reuse the existing Cockpit content views and read/context semantics; no redesign is included.\\n\\n## 2. UX Intent And Success\\n\\n- ui_ux_impact: medium\\n- ux_intent_definition: UX_INTENT_DEFINITION.md; ready analytical input recorded by operation 5df7c8fb-4ef2-44a7-8fdd-3f14d1e62630\\n- primary_user_intent: Install AGDF once and open its Cockpit without setting up another server.\\n- success_signal: In a fresh Codex session, the installed plugin opens the Cockpit and displays canonical data for the intended project, with a verified single effective Cockpit path after legacy transition.\\n- primary_decision_or_action: Ask to open Cockpit; supply a project only when the conversation has not already established one unambiguously.\\n\\n## 3. Working Modes And Effective State\\n\\n| working_mode | effective_state | visible_state_types | effective_state_authority | primary_state_presentation_owner |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Clean install or update | Plugin supplies compatible Cockpit assets; discovery may require a fresh session | Installed, reconnect needed, available, preparation failed | Host installation/activation and existing AGDF runtime verification | Existing installer output and Codex plugin/MCP management |\\n| Open for confirmed project | A checked project binding and current source reads are established | Cockpit ready for named project, opening failed | Existing AGDF target and canonical read services | Cockpit tool result and existing view |\\n| Project unresolved or unavailable | No project data can be presented as a valid binding | Project needed, project unavailable, retry available | Existing AGDF target validation | Cockpit tool result; concise chat clarification on" sandboxId=source-66635fa41555d0fc sourceId=undefined
